---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy · Asadullah Faisal" description="What this site does with your data: nothing leaves your device.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>This site has no analytics, no cookies, no trackers, and loads no third-party fonts or scripts.</p>
    <p>
      Some pages learn what you seem interested in (which cards you open, how long you read) so they can
      order the rest of the page for you. That happens entirely in your browser. It is saved only in your
      browser's local storage, never sent anywhere, and you can wipe it at any time with "Reset what this site
      learned".
    </p>
    <p>
      The photo demo and "Ask about me" run their models on your device. Your photos and questions are never
      uploaded. The model files are downloaded from this site the first time you use them and then kept in your
      browser's cache.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Recognizing the words inside a detected box would need a server. That is not part of the site yet; if it is
      added, the site will ask before sending a photo, and the server will not store it.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/">← Back</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding-top: 3rem; }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) { .page { padding-top: 5rem; } }
</style>
